<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        ADDED 2026-08-20 (disposition-tranche-2-requirements.md, D6.1) - BUYER ACTIVITY TIMELINE,
        SCHEMA HALF. ROLE-NAMED CONTACT LOOKUP, explicitly permitted by ARCHITECTURE.md §1 (a
        second Contact lookup on one object cannot both be Contact__c, so the field name carries
        the role).

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 DELIBERATELY UNFILTERED. DO NOT ADD Is_Buyer__c. THIS WAS AN OPEN DESIGN ITEM (O-5),
        NOW CLOSED BY THE USER'S ACCEPTED RECOMMENDATION - DO NOT RE-OPEN IT.
        =====================================================================================
        Six Contact lookups in this repo (Broker_Assignment__c.Broker__c,
        Disposition__c.Broker__c, Lease_Inquiry__c.Broker__c, BOV_Submission__c.Broker__c,
        BOV_Broker_Change__c.Incoming_Broker__c / Outgoing_Broker__c) carry an ACTIVE,
        non-optional lookupFilter selecting the Contact.Broker RECORD TYPE.

        🔴 TWO CORRECTIONS, 2026-08-20, quoted rather than deleted:

          RETRACTED: "Every other Contact lookup in this repo (... Opportunity.Broker__c ...)
          carries an ACTIVE, non-optional lookupFilter on Contact.Is_Broker__c."
        (a) It is not EVERY other one. Opportunity.Broker__c has NO <lookupFilter> element at
        all - verified twice by reading that file in full - so it is removed from the list
        above. Three other files in this repo repeat the same false claim. It is deliberately
        staying unfiltered: it is machine-stamped by LeadConvertService, and a non-optional
        filter there would make lead conversion fail hard. User-decided, do not re-open.
        (b) The predicate is no longer Contact.Is_Broker__c. The broker definition moved to the
        Contact.Broker record type on 2026-08-20 (measured: ZERO Contacts carried the checkbox,
        19 sat on the record type). The argument below is UNAFFECTED - it is about whether
        "buyer" is a durable role, not about how "broker" is spelled - so read
        "Is_Broker__c works because..." as "the broker record type works because...".

        This one intentionally does not, for a reason specific to what "buyer" means here:
          1. The broker filter works because a broker is a DURABLE role - the same Contact brokers
             many deals over years, and scripts/seed-broker-contacts.apex maintains that
             population. A buyer is DEAL-SCOPED: the counterparty on one sale, often a one-time
             principal created AT THE MOMENT the NDA is opened.
          2. An active, non-optional filter would force the analyst to tick a checkbox on a
             brand-new Contact before they can name them on an NDA mid-negotiation, with a
             refusal message naming an internal field.
          3. There is NO POPULATION TO FILTER AGAINST. Is_Broker__c was added with a seed script
             behind it; a hypothetical Is_Buyer__c would read false on 100% of Contacts on day
             one, and the lookup would offer nothing to pick.
        If scoping is ever wanted, the documented fallback is an isOptional=true lookupFilter (a
        suggestion, not a refusal) - never an active one, and never without a seed/backfill story
        first.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 NDA__c IS A DUAL-MODULE OBJECT. THIS FIELD IS INERT ON THE ACQUISITION SIDE.
        =====================================================================================
        NDA__c serves Acquisitions as well as Dispositions (both record types share this object).
        This field carries no record-type restriction and is technically settable on an
        acquisition NDA, but it is deliberately NOT added to any acquisition-specific
        permission set (DPEG_Acquisition_Edit / DPEG_Acquisition_View) or layout in this change -
        it ships FLS-invisible there, which is the safe default until an acquisition use case is
        actually requested.

        =====================================================================================
        RELATIONSHIP NAME: Buyer_NDAs. COLLISION CHECKED, NOT ASSUMED.
        =====================================================================================
        Every referenceTo Contact field in this repo as of this change uses one of
        Broker_Assignments, Brokered_Dispositions, Lease_Inquiries, Brokered_Opportunities,
        Brokered_BOV_Submissions, Incoming_Broker_Changes or Outgoing_Broker_Changes.
        Buyer_NDAs is free.

        =====================================================================================
        LABEL: "Buyer Contact", NOT "Buyer". CHECKED AGAINST EVERY EXISTING NDA__c FIELD LABEL.
        =====================================================================================
        No field on NDA__c is labelled "Buyer" today (Party_Role__c carries a PICKLIST VALUE
        labelled "Buyer", a different namespace entirely - field labels and picklist value labels
        never collide in the UI, but the two sitting side by side on the same edit form would
        still read ambiguously). "Buyer Contact" is unique on this object and mirrors the label
        chosen for Disposition_Offer__c.Buyer__c in the same change, where "Buyer" IS already
        taken by Buyer_Name__c.

        deleteConstraint SetNull, matching every sibling Contact lookup in this repo - deleting a
        buyer Contact must never delete the NDA that is evidence of what they signed or refused.

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 FLS: THIS FIELD IS INVISIBLE TO EVERYONE, ADMINS INCLUDED, UNTIL A PERMSET LANDS.
        =====================================================================================
        A Metadata API deployed custom field arrives with NO field permissions for any profile,
        System Administrator included. Read and edit are granted in DPEG_Disposition_Edit and
        read only in DPEG_Disposition_View in the same change - the two permission sets that
        already carry every other NDA__c business field. Neither DPEG_Acquisition_Edit,
        DPEG_Acquisition_View nor DPEG_Admin_Access is touched (see the dual-module note above).
        This file and those two permission sets must deploy together.
    -->
    <fullName>Buyer__c</fullName>
    <deleteConstraint>SetNull</deleteConstraint>
    <description>Buyer contact for this NDA. Deliberately UNFILTERED - see in-file comment; no Is_Buyer__c gate exists. NDA__c also serves Acquisitions; this field is inert there and is not granted on any acquisition permission set or layout.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Pick the buyer Contact this NDA is with. Not filtered by role - a buyer is often a brand-new Contact created for this deal.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Buyer Contact</label>
    <referenceTo>Contact</referenceTo>
    <relationshipLabel>Buyer NDAs</relationshipLabel>
    <relationshipName>Buyer_NDAs</relationshipName>
    <required>false</required>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Lookup</type>
</CustomField>
